Added identity linking. `GET @identities` lists the identities you own, `POST @identities` starts a flow that attaches another provider to your account, and `DELETE @identities/<provider>/<subject>` unlinks one unless it is your last way in. A linking flow requires an authenticated session at initiation *and* completion by the same session: an attempt records whose account it is for, and the callback refuses to finish it as anybody else — even for a browser holding the code, the state and the flow cookie. An identity already owned by another userid is a hard error with an audit entry, never a merge. @ericof
